This repository contains no source code from openai/math.

`recheck.sh` fetches the files it checks directly from
https://github.com/openai/math at a pinned commit
(adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a) into an untracked `.work/`
directory. Those files are:

    Copyright OpenAI
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/LICENSE

The short excerpts that appear in the README files of this repository — the
statement of `UniversalBound`, the two theorem signatures, and the five
definitions they depend on — are quoted for the purpose of identifying what is
being checked.

`families/*/Verify.lean` deliberately re-declares the definitions from the
corresponding `ComparatorChallenges` file verbatim. That is not incidental
copying: the whole point of the definitional-equality gate is that the two
declarations are textually identical, and `audit.sh` gate D fails if they ever
drift apart.

Mathlib4 (https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4) and the Lean 4
toolchain are downloaded by `lake` and `elan` at the revisions pinned by
upstream; both are Apache-2.0.
